[housing] agent_start: Housing: Find a reentry or transitional bed for a single man on parole in Oakland/Alameda County that can take him before the end of the month (sober living, reentry housing, or a parolee program such as STOP or a CDCR-funded bed through his parole agent). Also find longer-term affordable or rapid-rehousing programs that lead to his own apartment. List intake steps and any waitlists.
[legal_id] agent_start: Legal, ID & money: 1) Get a replacement Social Security card: find the nearest SSA office to Oakland 94607 and list what to bring (his state ID) and whether he needs an appointment. 2) Find second-chance banking: a free or low-fee checking account he can open with a state ID, and how to check whether a ChexSystems record would block him. 3) Find a free record-relief consultation (e.g. Alameda County Public Defender Clean Slate, East Bay Community Law Center) about relief for his property conviction after parole, and about any certificate-of-rehabilitation path.
[food_benefits] agent_start: Food & benefits: Help him apply for CalFresh with expedited (within 3 days) issuance, plus Alameda County General Assistance cash aid. List the nearest Social Services office or online application (BenefitsCal) and drop-in food pantries or free meals near 94607 to cover him until benefits arrive. Mention transit fare help (e.g. a reduced-fare Clipper card).
[health] agent_start: Health & recovery: Enroll him in Medi-Cal (Alameda County) and connect him to a primary care clinic near West Oakland that serves people after release (e.g. a federally qualified health center or Transitions Clinic). Include where he can get an occupational or physical exam if an employer or forklift program requires one.
[jobs] agent_start: Jobs & training: Find warehouse and logistics jobs (day or swing shifts) open to people with records in Alameda County, plus free or low-cost forklift certification programs (e.g. a reentry job-training program, Workforce Development Board / AJCC funding, Cypress Mandela, Oakland Private Industry Council). Focus on fair-chance employers near the Port of Oakland, Hayward and San Leandro that he can reach by transit.
